From 230a0a81bfeb7654e998425f1f74e4c088e69144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ananth <ananth.chellappa@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:55:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] subckt.c: bin in double, with the same test as INPgetModBin()

Under ngbehavior=hsa a multi-finger size on an inner bin edge stops the
load with "could not find a valid modelname", since 03ef19244 made the
binner apply min <= size < max.  With w=15u nf=5 one finger is exactly
3u, which belongs in the card with wmin=3u, on these bins:

    .model card.2 nmos ... wmin=3e-6 wmax=1.01e-3
    .model card.1 nmos ... wmin=4.2e-7 wmax=3e-6

The expander in doit() drops the .model cards whose bin does not hold
the size on the x line, and compares in float.  (float)15e-6 / 5 is
below (float)3e-6, or (float)1e-6 * 15 / 5 with .option scale=1u, so it
drops card.2 and keeps card.1.  INPgetModBin() then works in double and
rightly rejects card.1, and no card is left.

Export the binner's test as INPbinInRange() and call it from the
expander, so the two stages cannot disagree on a size.  The expander
and the w, l, nf of struct card become double.  A size off an edge keeps
its card, and a size on the outermost max stays rejected.

The test binning-hsa.cir sets ngbehavior in its .control section and
gives the circuit with circbyline, so it needs no .spiceinit.  It has
two finger sizes on inner edges and two off any edge, without and with
.option scale, and compares each with a plain model.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
